WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.8 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
HR and workplace policies

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
As soon as anyone helps, even one volunteer, you need some workplace policies.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
HR and workplace policies set out how you treat the people who work with you, paid or unpaid. You need some as soon as anyone helps, and employment law will require more once you employ people.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
Two groups, kept apart

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:41.574
Volunteers: A lighter but real framework: role descriptions, expenses, supervision, conduct and how concerns are handled. For example: Friends helping at the Saturday stall get a role description and an expenses form.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:54.104
Employees: Policies the law requires: recruitment, pay, hours, leave, grievance, discipline, health and safety. For example: Before the four paid trainees start: contracts, hours, leave and kitchen safety rules.

7
00:00:54.504 --> 00:00:55.104
Why it matters early

8
00:00:55.104 --> 00:01:00.407
1. Volunteer documents that look like employment can create legal duties.

9
00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:05.341
2. Clear rules protect both the people and the initiative.

10
00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:12.015
3. Policies ready before the first person joins mean no improvising later.

11
00:01:12.415 --> 00:01:13.015
Where it fits

12
00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:18.689
1. Your people plans from Module 4: recruitment, onboarding, pay and culture.

13
00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:25.104
2. Your policy register: an owner, a review date and a trigger for each.

14
00:01:25.104 --> 00:01:30.296
3. Checks by a qualified local employment adviser.

15
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:31.296
What to avoid

16
00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:36.230
Assuming friends who help need no framework at all.

17
00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:41.163
Paying volunteers small amounts without checking where employment begins.

18
00:01:41.163 --> 00:01:46.726
Using templates without adapting them to local law.

19
00:01:47.326 --> 00:01:49.126
You list the HR policies you will need, their triggers and status.

20
00:01:49.126 --> 00:01:53.126
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

21
00:01:54.626 --> 00:01:57.726
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
